<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">White Lotus Rebellion</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1796–1804</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/white-lotus">White Lotus</a> Rebellion was a large uprising in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> from 1796 to 1804, inspired by White Lotus millenarian teachings and fuelled by poverty, population pressure and official corruption. It took years and great expense for the Qing to suppress. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a> treat it as an early sign of the dynasty's decline and of the weakness of its regular armies.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/white-lotus-rebellion.jpg" alt="White Lotus Rebellion" width="320" height="138" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anonymous (Qing dynasty) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_portrait_of_the_White_Lotus_rebellion.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
